<div class="markup-toc-wrapper">
<button class="markup-toc-button">Show Table of Contents</button></div>Welcome to Wowhead's Best in Slot Gear list for Holy Paladin Healer in Cataclysm Classic Phase 4. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from Dragon Soul, Firelands, Twilight Protocol Dungeons, and Valor Points. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">
<span class="c2">Best in Slot Gear for Holy Paladin Healer in Phase 4</span></h2>In this final phase of Cataclysm gear choices are relatively straight foward; near exclusively when choosing between two pieces of gear the answer is to pick the item with the high item level. Due to <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/guide/item-reforging-overview">reforging</a>, many items are still functionally very equivalent to each other and any difference between item rankings amounts to minor optimizations at best. Nonetheless, as a general rule of thumb, you should prioritize high ilvl pieces with spirit or haste as secondary stats, (preferably both). As a refresher, the Holy Paladin general stat priority is as follows:<ol>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Intellect - Intellect directly provides spellpower as well as mana and crit. It is worth up to twice as much as some secondary stats, and should generally be the primary focus when choosing gear.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Spirit - Due to the prevelance of casting <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=82327/holy-radiance">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_paladin_divinecircle.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Holy Radiance</span></a> in the raid setting, Holy Paladin is a very mana-hungry spec. When considering Pre-Bis gear, (as opposed to full Raid-BiS), it is generally the correct decision to always go for more spirit over other secondaries, except perhaps Haste.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Haste - Once mana concerns are addressed, Haste is the main throughput secondary stat. At this point of the expansion, players may find they are able to sacrifice some Spirit to gain more Haste, dependent on the difficulty of content they are primarily interested in.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Critical Strike - Mastery and Crit are similarly unattractive for Holy Paladins in Cataclysm, and the choice between them can be rather arbitrary. In general, critical strike is more likely to be valuable during <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=5892/dragon-soul">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Dragon Soul</span></a> encounters than Mastery, due to the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=82327/holy-radiance">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_paladin_divinecircle.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Holy Radiance</span></a> heavy style of healing required.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Mastery - Mastery works similar to Val'anyr in WotLK, adding a small shield to the recipients of your heals, (though it notably does not apply to <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=53563/beacon-of-light">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_beaconoflight.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Beacon of Light</span></a>, lowering its value significantly). While objectively the lowest output stat, some players find that prioritizing Mastery allows for a more enjoyable playstyle – though it should be stressed that this is a strictly an inferior method of playing the class.</div></li></ol>
